 # DN_step_map
 
-Also called: Amanatides & Woo Ray Traversal, Digital Differential Analyzer raycast, Voxel Grid Raycasting (DDA), Voxel Raycasting / 3D DDA Block Traversal
+Also called: Amanatides-Woo Algorithm, Amanatides and Woo algorithm, Voxel DDA, DDA Voxel Traversal
 
 ## Overview
-DN_step_map is a voxel traversal algorithm that determines the sequence of voxels intersected by a ray in a regular grid without performing explicit intersection tests with voxel faces [S1, S2, S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently querying sparse or dense voxel structures for collision, occlusion, or surface detection by stepping through the grid along the ray direction [S6, unofficial]. It differs from fixed-step raymarching by using precomputed distance-to-boundary parameters (`tMax`) to jump directly to the next voxel boundary, ensuring exactly one voxel is processed per step and eliminating redundant checks [S6, unofficial]. It builds on [Voxel Raycasting with Normal Estimation](3901-voxel-raycasting-with-normal-estimation.md) by providing the core traversal mechanism that identifies the hit voxel and entry face, which are then used for normal estimation [S3, S6, unofficial].
+DN_step_map is a voxel traversal algorithm that determines the sequence of voxels intersected by a ray in a regular grid without performing explicit intersection tests with voxel faces [S1, unofficial][S2][S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently querying sparse or dense voxel structures for collision, occlusion, or surface detection by stepping through the grid along the ray direction [S6, unofficial]. It differs from fixed-step raymarching by using precomputed distance-to-boundary parameters (`tMax`) to jump directly to the next voxel boundary, ensuring exactly one voxel is processed per step and eliminating redundant checks [S6, unofficial]. It builds on [Voxel Raycasting with Normal Estimation](3901-voxel-raycasting-with-normal-estimation.md) by providing the core traversal mechanism that identifies the hit voxel and entry face, which are then used for normal estimation [S6, S7, unofficial].
 
