 ## Background
-The algorithm is based on the Amanatides & Woo method, originally published in 1986 for ray tracing through voxel grids [S1, S2, unofficial]. It is widely implemented in voxel engines for efficient raycasting [S6, S7, unofficial]. Variants are used in game development for terrain interaction and in scientific visualization for volume rendering [S3, unofficial][S5].
